  <pre><code><span class="cm"># Ensure complete reproducibility</span>
<span class="kw">import</span> os
<span class="kw">import</span> numpy <span class="kw">as</span> np
<span class="kw">import</span> tensorflow <span class="kw">as</span> tf

<span class="cm"># Set seeds FIRST, before any randomness</span>
SEED <span class="op">=</span> <span class="nm">42</span>
os.<span class="fn">environ</span>[<span class="st">'PYTHONHASHSEED'</span>] <span class="op">=</span> <span class="fn">str</span>(SEED)
np.random.<span class="fn">seed</span>(SEED)
tf.random.<span class="fn">set_seed</span>(SEED)

<span class="cm"># Optional: enable deterministic GPU operations (slower)</span>
os.<span class="fn">environ</span>[<span class="st">'TF_DETERMINISTIC_OPS'</span>] <span class="op">=</span> <span class="st">'1'</span>

<span class="cm"># Load data with fixed split</span>
<span class="va">train_data</span> <span class="op">=</span> load_data_v2_3_0()
<span class="va">indices</span> <span class="op">=</span> np.arange(<span class="fn">len</span>(<span class="va">train_data</span>))
np.random.<span class="fn">shuffle</span>(<span class="va">indices</span>)  <span class="cm"># Shuffled but seeded!</span></code></pre>
  <div class="code-explain">
    <p><strong>What is happening:</strong> We set all random seeds before any imports of randomness-using libraries. We enable deterministic GPU operations (with performance cost). We shuffle data but in a seeded, reproducible way.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="key-takeaway">
    <h4>✦ Key Takeaways</h4>
    <ul>
      <li>Reproducibility requires seeding ALL sources of randomness</li>
      <li>Version and hash all input data; store checksums</li>
      <li>Lock all dependencies (pip freeze, conda export)</li>
      <li>Document exact preprocessing transformations</li>
      <li>Test reproducibility: run pipeline twice, verify identical outputs</li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</section>

