<!-- ===== SECTION 3: AUDIT TRAILS AND COMPLIANCE ===== -->
<section class="section reveal" id="audit-compliance">
  <span class="section-label">Governance Framework</span>
  <h2>Audit Trails and Regulatory Compliance</h2>

  <p>An audit trail is a chronological record answering: Who? What? When? Where? Why? and How? In production AI, this means tracking every model change, deployment, inference, and decision boundary adjustment. For regulated industries, this is non-negotiable. For all organizations, it's business intelligence.</p>

  <p>Modern compliance frameworks (GDPR, HIPAA, SOX, AI Act) all require extensive logging. You need to be able to answer: "This customer's data was used in training model v2.3.1. Who had access? When was it trained? What consent was given? How can we delete it?"</p>

