<!-- ===== SECTION 4: MODEL GOVERNANCE POLICIES ===== -->
<section class="section reveal" id="governance-policies">
  <span class="section-label">Operational Excellence</span>
  <h2>Model Governance Policies and Approval Gates</h2>

  <p>Governance policies define the rules for model development, testing, and deployment. They answer: What must pass before a model goes to production? Who can approve changes? What metrics must be met? What happens if something fails? Without clear policies, decisions become inconsistent and reactive.</p>

  <p>Effective governance balances safety with velocity. You want enough checks to catch problems, but not so many that innovation stops. The solution is risk-based governance: higher-stakes decisions require more oversight, while low-risk experiments can move fast.</p>

